          %title
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Dirac"} Wikipedia entry
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            Early discussion of the foundations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            (including the possibly first consideration of what came to be known as the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Slater+determinant"} Slater determinant
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+A.+M.+Dirac"}> Paul A. M. Dirac
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the theory of quantum mechanics
              %strong 112
              762 (1926) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1926.0133"}> doi:10.1098/rspa.1926.0133
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and with early emphasis of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Born-Pauli+rule"} Born-Pauli rule
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+A.+M.+Dirac"}> Paul A. M. Dirac
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The physical interpretation of the quantum dynamics
              %strong 113
              765 (1927) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1927.0012"}> doi:10.1098/rspa.1927.0012
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Introducing what came to be called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+flux+quantization"}> flux quantization
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            and its potential
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+monopole"} magnetic monopole
            sources:
          %ul
            %li#Dirac31
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/P.A.M.+Dirac"}> P.A.M. Dirac
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantized Singularities in the Electromagnetic Field
              %strong 133
              821 (1931) 60-72 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1931.0130"}> doi:10.1098/rspa.1931.0130
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Precursor discussion to the
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+A.+M.+Dirac"}> Paul A. M. Dirac
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Lagrangian in Quantum Mechanics
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 3
              = succeed "&rbrack;," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.informationphilosopher.com/solutions/scientists/dirac/Lagrangian_1933.pdf"} pdf
              %a{:href => "path+integral#Brown05"} Brown 2005
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789812567635_0003"}> doi:10.1142/9789812567635_0003
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Introducing
            = succeed "-notation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bra-ket"} bra-ket
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
          %ul
            %li#Dirac39
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+A.+M.+Dirac"}> Paul A. M. Dirac
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A new notation for quantum mechanics
              %strong 35
              3 (1939) 416-418 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100021162"}> doi:10.1017/S0305004100021162
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ifsc.usp.br/~lattice/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/Dirac_notation.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Introducing the modern theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constrained+mechanics"} constrained
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+mechanics"} Hamiltonian mechanics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+A.+M.+Dirac"}> Paul A. M. Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Hamiltonian Dynamics
                %strong 2
                (1950) 129-148 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4153/CJM-1950-012-1"}> doi:10.4153/CJM-1950-012-1
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %p reprinted in:
              %p
                Alexander S. Blum,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dean+Rickles"} Dean Rickles
                (eds.), Ch.34 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Gravity in the First Half of the Twentieth Century: A Sourcebook
                %strong 10
                (2018) 484-503 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://edition-open-sources.org/sources/10/"}> doi:10.34663/9783945561317-00
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://edition-open-sources.org/media/sources/10/36/sources10chap34.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+membrane"} relativistic membrane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
          %ul
            %li#Dirac62
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Extensible Model of the Electron
                %strong 268
                (1962) 57-67 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2414316"}> jstor:2414316
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (also proposing the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac-Born-Infeld+action"} Dirac-Born-Infeld action
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The motion of an Extended Particle in the Gravitational Field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leopold+Infeld"} L. Infeld
                (ed.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Relativistic Theories of Gravitation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1623740"} spire:1623740
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Dirac-MotionOfAnExtendedParticle.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/2282975/files/warsaw-1962.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Particles of Finite Size in the Gravitational Field
                %strong 270
                (1962) 354-356 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1962.0228"}> doi:10.1098/rspa.1962.0228
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            (and some
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %ul
            %li#Dirac30
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Principles+of+Quantum+Mechanics"} The Principles of Quantum Mechanics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-principles-of-quantum-mechanics-9780198520115"} ISBN:9780198520115
            %li#Dirac78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The mathematical foundations of quantum theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Theory
          %p
            Early discussion of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positron"} positron
          %ul
            %li#Dirac33
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+A.+M.+Dirac"}> Paul A. M. Dirac
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Théorie du Positron
              = succeed "," do
                %em Structure et propriétés des noyaux atomiques
              %a{:href => "http://www.solvayinstitutes.be/"} Solvay
              Conference (1933) 203-212 &amp;lbrack;full:
              %a{:href => "http://www.solvayinstitutes.be/pdf/Proceedings_Physics/1933.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h2#quotes Quotes
          %p#OnNotation
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
          %blockquote
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Dirac39"}> Dirac 1939
              \&amp;rbrack; In mathematical theories the question of notation, while not of primary importance, is yet worthy of careful consideration, since a good notation can be of great value in helping the development of a theory, by making it easy to write down those quantities or combinations of quantities that are important, and difficult or impossible to write down those that are unimportant.
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
          %blockquote
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Dirac78"}> Dirac 1978
              \:&amp;rbrack; One should keep the need for a sound mathematical basis dominating one’s search for a new theory. Any physical or philosophical ideas that one has must be adjusted to fit the mathematics. Not the way round.
            %p Too many physicists are inclined to start from some preconceived physical ideas and then to try to develop them and ﬁnd a mathematical scheme that incorporates them. Such a line of attack is unlikely to lead to success. One runs into difficulties and ﬁnds no reasonable way out of them. One ought then to realize that one’s whole line of approach is wrong and to seek a new starting point with a sound mathematical basis.
          %p On anxiety with new ideas:
          %blockquote
            %p I think he [Heisenberg] failed to make this discovery simply because he was too scared. He was afraid of his own bold new idea, and he was afraid that if he went too far with it, it might all break down.
            %p I had a great advantage over Heisenberg. I did not have any of these fears, because it was not my idea. I could play about with this non-commuting algebra… and see where it led
